### Peticiones de api (REST Client de VS Code o compatible)
### Requiere auth en :8080 y api en :8000. El token se obtiene con el login de abajo.

@authUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1) Login: guarda el token para las demás peticiones
# @name login
POST {{authUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "student",
  "password": "Workshop123!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Listar tareas del usuario autenticado -> 200
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Crear tarea -> 201
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Probar con .http",
  "description": "Tarea creada desde docs/api.http",
  "status": "TODO",
  "priority": "HIGH"
}

### Resumen de tareas -> 200 { owner, total, byStatus, highPriorityOpen }
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Subir requerimiento (multipart) -> 201 { owner, fileName, storedAt, size }
POST {{apiUrl}}/api/requirements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LabBoundary

--LabBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="requirements.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

El login debe ser accesible.
--LabBoundary--

### Salud del backend auth vista desde api -> 200
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/backend-health
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sin token -> 401 { "detail": "Invalid token" }
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/tasks

### Token inválido -> 401
GET {{apiUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer no-es-un-jwt
